Big thanks to EA for
sponsoring this video.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.450
We're here to promote "Battlefield 1".

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.520
Dan, what do you like
about the first World War,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.353
the Great War?

00:00:23.353 --> 00:00:25.170
It's the amount of tech that was made.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.720
As a kid I never
understood how they managed

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.210
to do the thing where
they fired machine guns

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.380
through the propellers of planes.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.400
I just didn't understand it.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.233
The old sync gear.

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:34.910
Yeah, and now I'm a grown-up
and I thought, you know,

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.200
the internet has been invented
I'm gonna have to look it up,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.720
and they have something called
sync gear like you said,

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.080
where the bullets managed

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.000
to just go in between the propellers,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.580
and so they could fly the plane

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.620
and shoot where they're looking at

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.450
as opposed to trying to control a gun

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.580
and the plane at the same time,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.680
which I imagine is really hard.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.310
Well it's very difficult
to find a World War I plane

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.130
that still shoots live ammo
through its own propeller,

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.230
but thankfully we've been able to

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.290
recreate exactly that with this device,

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.610
and we're gonna film it
at extremely high speeds.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.360
I whipped this up last night,
I can't wait to get on it.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.193
You made this, did you?

00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:08.470
Yeah, yeah I made it with a
hammer, screwdriver, spanner.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.303
Phillip's head?

00:01:09.303 --> 00:01:10.200
Yeah, yeah Phillip's head.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.270
